<title>ITALY: Italy's Naples sees April CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Naples sees April CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Naples said its April consumer price index stood at 0.3 percent month on month and 2.8 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In March, Naples' inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 2.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Naples is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data Monday and Tuesday. The city's CPI weighs 6.64 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes:</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to March 1997)</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   0.3    (0.1)     2.5  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Food				0.3    (0.0)     2.4  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.1    (0.1)     1.7  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Housing/utility charges     0.6   (-0.1)     2.0  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.1    (0.2)     1.6  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Health services		 0.0    (0.1)     2.7  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Transportation		  0.0    (0.1)     3.9  (4.7)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  -0.2   (-0.2)     2.3  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Education			 0.0    (0.4)     4.1  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	0.7    (0.0)     3.5  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Other goods and services    0.5    (0.5)     2.3  (2.1)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
